  @service('bar-config') barConfig;

  setupController(controller, model) {
    super.setupController(controller, model);
    this.barConfig.title = 'User Profile';
    this.barConfig.height = 60; // 60px tall
  }
}
```

```hbs
<!-- app/templates/profile.hbs -->
<Bar />
<p>Here is the user profile.</p>
```

**How it works**

1. **`bar-config` service** – holds the current bar title and height.  
2. **`Bar` component** – reads the service and renders a `<div>` with the configured height and title.  
3. **Routes (`dashboard`, `profile`)** – in `setupController` they set the service’s `title` and `height` values.  
4. **Templates** – simply include `<Bar />`; the component automatically reflects the current route’s configuration.  

Add the files above to your Ember CLI project, run `ember serve`, and navigate to `/dashboard` or `/profile` to see the bar update accordingly.

