unshiftObject method is not working in ember.

I have the array of Objects and want to concat only the list property of all objects and create a new array. So I have a "combinedList" getter in the below code to combine the list if array length is greater than 1 else just return the 1st items list property. This returned array will be used in the template file to display. If any new item is added, the addComment function will be called with the newly added item and push that to the "combinedList" array.
The problem here is, if the objArr length is less than 1, the newItem is pushed to the "combineList". But, if it is greater than 1, newItem is not pushed to the "combinedList" array.
Can anyone please help me to figure out the cause for this issue?
export default class YourComponent extends Component {
 objArr = [ {id:1, list:[1,2,3]}, {id:2, list:[3,4]} ];

 get combinedList() {
 if (this.objArr.length > 1) {
 let list = [];
 this.objArr.forEach((item) => {
 list.push(...item.list);
 });
 return list;
 }
 return this.objArr[0].list;
 }

 // Call this method when adding a new item
 addComment(newItem) {
 this.combinedList.unshiftObject(newItem);
 }
}

response_prompt:
`combinedList` is a **getter** that creates a new array every time it is read.  
When you call

```js
this.combinedList.unshiftObject(newItem);
```

you are mutating that temporary array – the mutation is lost as soon as the
getter finishes, and the value is never stored back into `objArr`.  
In addition, the array returned by the getter is a plain JavaScript array, so
`unshiftObject` (an Ember‑Array method) is undefined.

**Fix**

Keep the combined list in a tracked property (or update `objArr` and let the
getter recompute) and use Ember’s array mutation helpers.

```js
import Component from '@glimmer/component';
import { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking';
import { A } from '@ember/array';

export default class YourComponent extends Component {
  // The source array – use EmberArray so we can mutate it
  @tracked objArr = A([
    { id: 1, list: [1, 2, 3] },
    { id: 2, list: [3, 4] }
  ]);

  // A tracked array that holds the concatenated values
  @tracked combinedList = this._buildCombinedList();

  // Re‑build the combined list whenever objArr changes
  _buildCombinedList() {
    if (this.objArr.length > 1) {
      return this.objArr.reduce((acc, item) => acc.concat(item.list), []);
    }
    return this.objArr[0]?.list ?? [];
  }

  // Call this when adding a new item
  addComment(newItem) {
    // Add the new item to the source array
    this.objArr.pushObject(newItem);

    // Re‑compute the combined list
    this.combinedList = this._buildCombinedList();
  }
}
```

Now `combinedList` is a real tracked array that you can mutate with
`unshiftObject`, `pushObject`, etc., and the template will update
automatically.

